    "description": "An order-management platform consumes a single stream of business events (order created, payment captured, shipment delayed, return requested) from a broker. Today one consumer function loads every message, inspects a type field and chains through if-elif to the right handler; shipment-delay handling was added last month and payment events started going to the return handler after a copy-paste mistake. Different event types need different validation, different downstream systems and different retry policies, and the operations team wants to add a channel for a new event type without editing the dispatch chain. The decision to implement: how to send each incoming event to the handler that owns its kind, decided from the message content, while keeping handlers independent and adding new kinds without editing existing routing.",
    "decision_statement": "Route each incoming event to the handler that owns its kind based on message content, without editing existing branches.",
    "notes": "Covered also by the flow-with-detour case; splitter stays acceptable for the multi-handler variant."
  },
